{title: MEMORY (In C)}
{subtitle: Elaine Paige-Betty Buckley}
Andrew Lloyd Webber wrote Memory with key changes so in order to keep friendly chord shapes you’ll have to move the capo where indicated.  Betty’s version starts with Capo 2 and then moves up to Capo 3 after the preamble.  Elaine begins with Capo 3.  Both versions move up three frets to Capo 6 prior to the second bridge.

     1st intro:  Form (C) and walk down the strings beginning with the 4th string (mid  <e>) to the 1st string (high <e>) and back up to the 3rd string and repeat.  Repeat and start the song with the (C).

     French horn part:  The French horn plays a series of notes as couplets or triplets.  It starts with note <f#> at the 4th string/4th fret and walks up (in pitch) to note <f> at the 1st string/1st fret and the retraces the notes as it walks back down to the <a> at the 3d string/2nd fret.  Repeat the squence being with the open 3rd string note <g>.

     2nd intro:  Pick the open strings shown and begin the song.

